BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Gravestone Stories - Alexandria Historic Cemetery Complex - 13 Cemeteries Walking Tour
DESCRIPTION:Go beyond King Street on a 90-minute guided walk through Alexandria's remarkable Wilkes Street Cemetery Complex&#x97\;13 historic cemeteries\, 52 acres\, and more than 35\,000 burials in one walkable landscape.\nLed by independent historian and cemetery superintendent David Heiby\, creator of Gravestone Stories\, the tour connects Alexandria's past to the American Revolution\, War of 1812\, Civil War\, Cold War\, and more. Meet George Washington's pallbearers\, Revolutionary War patriots\, Civil War soldiers\, a Soviet spy\, and others whose stories illuminate more than two centuries of Alexandria history.\nEvery stop is grounded in original research\, cemetery records\, and discoveries made within the complex\, including graves rediscovered after nearly 200 years.\nTours are limited to small groups. The 90-minute walk covers approximately 1 to 1.5 miles over historic cemetery paths and uneven terrain. Free parking is available.\nTours are offered Fridays and Saturdays at 1:00 p.m.\, with an additional Thursday tour at 3:30 p.m. Tickets are $30 per person and include the official Gravestone Stories companion e-book. See the Gravestone Stories website for current availability and booking.
URL:https://www.viator.com/tours/Virginia/Journey-Through-Americas-Most-Historic-Cemetery-Complex/d22229-5589637P1
DTSTART:20261022T153000
DTEND:20261022T170000
LOCATION:Hamilton Avenue & Wilkes Street
GEO:38.801642;-77.056728
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Hamilton Avenue & Wilkes Street;X-APPLE-RADIUS=49;X-TITLE=Gravestone Stories:geo:38.801642,-77.056728
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
