BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Lloyd House: Alexandria Cider Festival
DESCRIPTION:Alexandria Cider Festival Celebrate Virginia Cider Week with a special tasting event on the grounds of historic Lloyd House and on Queen Street in Old Town Alexandria. The event includes cider tastings\, a souvineir cider glass\, live music\, tavern games\, a food truck\, and a little history too! This year\, for the nations 250th anniversary\, the VA250 Movile Museum Experience ("Out of Many\, One") will be open on Queen Street during the event. Tickets $50 per person through November 1\, $55 November 2-20\, and $25 for designated drivers. Online sales end at noon on Friday\, November 20. After that\, tickets can be purchased at the door for $65. Dress for the weather - the event is outdoors! Festival open 1 to 5 p.m. Proceeds from the Cider Festival will benefit the Historic Alexandria Museums.Please note: You do not need to print tickets. Your name will be on the registration list for this event. DOGS ARE NOT PERMITTED (except guide dogs).Minimum Age: 21
URL:https://shop.alexandriava.gov/Events.aspx
DTSTART:20261121T130000
DTEND:20261121T170000
LOCATION:220 N. Washington Street
GEO:38.807227;-77.046754
