STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Llyod House: Lecture: "Opium Slavery" by Johnathan S. Jones
DESCRIPTION:Join us at Lloyd House for a series of lectures featuring local authors\, with the third featuring Jonathan S. Jones\, author of "Opium Slavery\, Civil War Veterans and America's First Opioid Crisis." During the Civil War\, the utility and widespread availability of opium and morphine made opiates essential to wartime medicine. After the war ended\, thousands of ailing soldiers became addicted\, or &#x93\;enslaved\,&#x94\; as nineteenth-century Americans phrased it. Veterans\, their families\, and communities struggled to cope with addiction's health and social consequences. Medical and government authorities compounded veterans' suffering and imbued the epidemic with cultural meaning by branding addiction as a matter of moral weakness\, unmanliness\, or mental infirmity. Framing addiction as &#x93\;opium slavery&#x94\; limited the efficacy of care and left many veterans to suffer needlessly for decades after the war ended. Drawing from veterans' firsthand accounts as well as mental asylum and hospital records\, government and medical reports\, newspaper coverage of addiction\, and advertisements\, Jonathan S. Jones unearths the poorly understood stories of opiate-addicted Civil War veterans in unflinching detail\, illuminating the war's traumatic legacies. In doing so\, Jones provides critical historical context for the modern opioid crisis\, which bears tragic resemblance to that of the post&#x96\;Civil War era. Tickets are $15 / $12 for Office of Historic Alexandria members and volunteers at Alexandriava.gov/Shop.
URL:https://shop.alexandriava.gov/Events.aspx
DTSTART:20261115T150000
DTEND:20261115T163000
LOCATION:220 N. Washington Street
GEO:38.807227;-77.046754
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=220 N. Washington Street;X-APPLE-RADIUS=49;X-TITLE=Lloyd House:geo:38.807227,-77.046754
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Lyceum: The Forces Awaken!
DESCRIPTION:The Forces Awaken! \nJoin us for "The Forces Awaken!" - An Evening of Philosophic Reveries! A Pageant of Modern Scientifical Recreations &amp\; Amusements! Grand Spectacle and Curious Demonstrations Revealing Unseen &amp\; Mysterious Forces of the Universe\, Will Be on Display Courtesy of: The Professor. Join veteran science educator and historian Dean Howarth (The Natural Philosopher\, LLC) for an evening of 19the-century science. Mr. Howarth will conduct experiments from the 19th century\, much like ones conducted at Lyceum Hall in Alexandria in the 1840s and 50s. Enjoy astounding and shocking (sometimes literally) demonstrations as you learn about the invisible forces that are all around us. Beer and wine for sale. Tickets available online at AlexandriaVa.gov/Shop.
URL:https://shop.alexandriava.gov/Events.aspx
DTSTART:20261112T190000
DTEND:20261112T200000
LOCATION:201 S. Washington Street
GEO:38.803764;-77.047586
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=201 S. Washington Street;X-APPLE-RADIUS=49;X-TITLE=Alexandria History Museum at The Lyceum:geo:38.803764,-77.047586
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Grown-Up Field Trip: Who Gets Remembered
DESCRIPTION:Grown-Up Field Trip: Who Gets Remembered \nWhy do we remember some people from history while others are forgotten? Step inside Gadsby's Tavern Museum for an interactive exploration of the people whose stories have been preserved&#x97\;and those whose stories are harder to find. Through historic spaces and primary sources\, we'll question who gets remembered\, who gets left out\, and how those choices shape our understanding of the past. This program is part of Historic Alexandria's monthly Grown-Up Field Trip series\, where adults can feed their curiosity by learning more about Alexandria's history together.Please note this program involves ascending and descending historic stairs. Seating is provided at each stop during the tour.
URL:https://shop.alexandriava.gov/Events.aspx
DTSTART:20261107T180000
DTEND:20261107T193000
LOCATION:134 N. Royal Street
GEO:38.805543;-77.043624
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=134 N. Royal Street;X-APPLE-RADIUS=49;X-TITLE=Gadsby's Tavern Museum:geo:38.805543,-77.043624
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Gadsby's Tavern Museum: Specialty Tour- Hamilton's BFF & Frenemies
DESCRIPTION:Specialty Tour: Hamilton's BFF &amp\; Frenemies \nInspired by the musical Hamilton\, learn how the paths of Washington\, Lafayette\, Jefferson\, Madison\, and Burr all intersected with this local tavern. Includes discussion of the issues they faced and how their choices impacted local citizens. Please note tour involves ascending and descending stairs. Arrive no later than 5 minutes prior to tour time to check in. No need to print tickets--your name will be on a list after purchasing.
