BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Lyceum: Legends of Spain - Candlelit Guitar Masterpieces with Piotr Pakhomkin
DESCRIPTION:Step out of the noise &#x97\; no phones\, no notifications\, no screens &#x97\; and into candlelit Spanish guitar music performed by Piotr Pakhomkin.For one evening\, classical guitarist Piotr Pakhomkin transforms The Lyceum into an old-world salon\, performing the great Spanish repertoire &#x97\; Albéniz\, Granados and Tárrega &#x97\; music built on legend\, longing\, and flamenco fire. Between pieces\, Pakhomkin shares the stories behind the music: the myths\, the composers' obsessions\, the Spain that inspired them.This isn't a concert you scroll through. It's 50 minutes of a single instrument in a room lit by candlelight\, followed by a chance to meet the artist and ask questions.Doors at 7:00 PM. Performance begins 7:30 PM sharp. Seating is limited.Piotr Pakhomkin is a classical guitarist trained under Manuel Barrueco at Peabody\, whose 2018 Carnegie Hall debut with the Chamber Orchestra of New York's Masterwork Series marked the start of a career the Financial Times has called that of a &#x93\;master guitarist.&#x94\; WYPR's Midday on the Arts introduced him on-air as a &#x93\;virtuoso.&#x94\; He has performed at the Kennedy Center's Terrace Theater\, Jordan Hall\, Panama's National Theater\, and the Phillips Collection. Pakhomkin is a winner of the 2016 Respighi International Soloist Competition and the 2012 Concurso Internacional de Guitarra in Mexico.
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/legends-of-spain-candlelit-guitar-masterpieces-tickets-1993956327050
