BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Washington Metropolitan Philharmonic Association: Landscapes of the Spirit
DESCRIPTION:LANDSCAPES OF THE SPIRITSunday\, March 21 | 3 pm | George Washington Masonic National MemorialAnna Binneweg\, Conductor| Laura Metcalf\, cello &amp\; Rupert Boyd\, guitar\nJoin us in reflection with Landscapes of the Spirit\, featuring Laura Metcalf on cello and Rupert Boyd on guitar. This program opens with the Peruvian Apu: A Tone Poem for Orchestra by Gabriela Lena Frank\, followed by the loving Anahata: Unbroken Heart for Cello and Guitar by Claire Assad\, and ending with the beautiful Symphony No. 6 in F Major\, Op. 68\, &#x93\;Pastoral&#x94\; by Ludwig van Beethoven.
URL:https://www.wmpamusic.org/concerts.html
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270321
LOCATION:101 Callahan Drive
GEO:38.807295;-77.064361
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=101 Callahan Drive;X-APPLE-RADIUS=49;X-TITLE=Washington Metropolitan Philharmonic Association:geo:38.807295,-77.064361
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Washington Metropolitan Philharmonic Association: Ritual & Renewal
DESCRIPTION:RITUAL &amp\; RENEWALSunday\, February 7 | 3 pm | George Washington Masonic National MemorialAnna Binneweg\, Conductor\nJoin WashMetPhil on a musical journey with Ritual &amp\; Renewal. This program opens with the progressive Montgomery Variations by Margaret Bonds\, followed by the touching Lyric for Strings by George Walker and The Firebird Suite by Igor Stravinsky\, ending with the one and only Boléro by Maurice Ravel.
URL:https://www.wmpamusic.org/concerts.html
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270207
LOCATION:101 Callahan Drive
GEO:38.807295;-77.064361
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=101 Callahan Drive;X-APPLE-RADIUS=49;X-TITLE=Washington Metropolitan Philharmonic Association:geo:38.807295,-77.064361
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Washington Metropolitan Philharmonic Association: Festival of Light
DESCRIPTION:FESTIVAL OF LIGHTSaturday\, December 12 | 7 pm |George Washington Masonic National MemorialAnna Binneweg\, Conductor Alexandria Choral Society | Kathryn Harsha\, Artistic Director\nCelebrate the holiday season with WashMetPhil and Alexandria Choral Society in Festival of Light. This program opens with the lovely Helios Overture\, Op. 17 by Carl Nielsen\, followed by the energetic Starburst by Jessie Montgomery\, the distinctly American Appalachian Spring Suite by Aaron Copland\, and Fantasia on Christmas Carols by Ralph Vaugh Williams\, bringing a little twist to Christmas carols you love and know\, and ending the program with the beautiful Illuminare by Elaine Hagenberg.
URL:https://www.wmpamusic.org/concerts.html
